      "text": "To evaluate \\(\\left\\lceil -\\sqrt{\\frac{49}{4}} \\right\\rceil\\), we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Simplify the expression inside the square root.\n2. Find the square root of the simplified expression.\n3. Apply the negative sign to the result.\n4. Apply the ceiling function to the result.\n\nLet's go through each step in detail.\n\nStep 1: Simplify the expression inside the square root.\n\\[\n\\frac{49}{4} = 12.25\n\\]\nSo, we need to find \\(\\sqrt{12.25}\\).\n\nStep 2: Find the square root of 12.25.\n\\[\n\\sqrt{12.25} = 3.5\n\\]\n\nStep 3: Apply the negative sign to the result.\n\\[\n-\\sqrt{12.25} = -3.5\n\\]\n\nStep 4: Apply the ceiling function to the result.\nThe ceiling function \\(\\left\\lceil x \\right\\rceil\\) gives the smallest integer greater than or equal to \\(x\\). For \\(x = -3.5\\), the smallest integer greater than or equal to \\(-3.5\\) is \\(-3\\).\n\nTherefore, \\(\\left\\lceil -3.5 \\right\\rceil = -3\\).\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-3}\n\\]",
